SIAT awake-mouse MRI: eight-subject analysis subset

Contents
--------
This subset contains one T2-weighted anatomical image and one selected long
BOLD run per subject (sub-01 through sub-08). Seven BOLD runs contain 240
volumes and one (sub-04) contains 300 volumes, with a repetition time of 2 s.
The included images are raw NIfTI exports, not preprocessed derivatives.
Short reverse-encoding reference scans are not included in this release subset.
The preparation archive retains those scans separately outside this dataset.

Acquisition metadata and limitations
------------------------------------
Signed PhaseEncodingDirection could not be reliably verified for these runs
and is omitted rather than inferred from sequence labels. TotalReadoutTime
was derived from EffectiveEchoSpacing * (ReconMatrixPE - 1), as documented
in the preparation audit. These fields do not establish phase-encoding polarity.
No corresponding fieldmaps are distributed in this subset.

All eight included BOLD runs are labelled task-rest. For sub-04, the depositor
confirmed a resting-state acquisition without stimulation. Its original
sequence name included 2MT, but no stimulus was delivered during this run.
The task label has been corrected accordingly; no stimulus events.tsv applies.
The depositor confirmed that all eight mice were male and that the included
BOLD runs were acquired awake, without anesthesia and without stimulation.
The depositor confirmed the strain as C57BL/6J. Age at scanning was not available during preparation and is not inferred
from surgery ages reported in related publications.

The depositor confirmed that the anatomical and functional images assigned
to sub-03 belong to the same animal but were acquired on two separate scan
occasions. The anatomical image is therefore a cross-scan reference for the
BOLD run, rather than an anatomical acquisition from the same scan occasion.
The exact scan dates and interval have not been confirmed in this preparation.

Ethics and preparation status
-----------------------------
The depositor confirmed that these eight mice are covered by ethics approval
SIAT-IACUC-240702-YGS-LY-A2838. The depositor-confirmed CC0 license and ordered
author list are retained from the source draft.
The previously flagged sub-03 animal identity and sub-04 experimental condition
have been clarified by the depositor. Age at scanning and the interval between
the two scan occasions for sub-03 were not provided. These omissions are
reported explicitly rather than filled with inferred values.
OpenNeuro accession: ds009028.
The preparation archive and audit records are retained separately from this release.
